{"text": "blueprint:\n  name: FLARE\n  description: >\n    FLARE: phase-based circadian lighting - sets brightness/colour\n    temperature from a FLARE schedule sensor,\n    keeping lights updated as it changes, and turns them off a while\n    after occupancy clears. Full details on every input:\n    [the blueprint reference](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/).\n\n\n    Blueprint version 0.16.0 - the integration raises a repair when a\n    newer one is available.\n  domain: automation\n  author: Dan Spencer\n  homeassistant:\n    # Required by the occupancy.* triggers/conditions.\n    min_version: 2026.4.0\n  input:\n    schedule:\n      name: Schedule\n      description: >\n        The FLARE schedule the room follows: the brightness and colour\n        temperature it applies.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        device:\n          filter:\n            - integration: flare\n              model: Schedule\n    zone:\n      name: Zone\n      description: >\n        The FLARE zone this room belongs to. It records which lights FLARE\n        is driving, so a light someone else changes is left alone. Leave it\n        empty to turn that off for this room.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      # Optional: without a zone the room isn't tracked, and ticks on the\n      # minute instead of the zone's spaced tick.\n      default: null\n      selector:\n        device:\n          filter:\n            - integration: flare\n              model: Zone\n    room_target:\n      name: Lights & Occupancy\n      description: >\n        Entity, device, area, floor, or label - lights within it are\n        controlled, occupancy and motion sensors within it decide when (see\n        Sensors From Areas, under Triggers).\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        target:\n          entity:\n            - domain: light\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: occupancy\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: motion\n    no_motion_wait:\n      name: Wait time\n      description: >\n        Only used when the room has occupancy or motion sensors: how long\n        every one must be clear before the room counts as empty and its\n        lights turn off.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      default: 120\n      selector:\n        number:\n          min: 0\n          max: 3600\n          unit_of_measurement: seconds\n    brightness_exclusions:\n      name: Brightness & Exclusions\n      icon: mdi:brightness-6\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        brightness_template:\n          name: Brightness Template (Optional)\n          description: >\n            Template returning entity_id \u2192 brightness, 0-255, replacing\n            the curve's brightness for the lights it names (0 = off, null\n            = skip entirely). The same scale the phase brightnesses use.\n            Its own per-entity values always win over the per-phase\n            exclusions below - those only fill in entities it doesn't\n            already mention.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, under Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#brightness).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Morning (Optional)\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        day_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Day (Optional)\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        evening_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Evening (Optional)\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        night_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off During Night (Optional)\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n    idle_brightness:\n      name: Idle Brightness\n      icon: mdi:lightbulb-night\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        idle_brightness_template:\n          name: Idle Brightness Template (Optional)\n          description: >\n            Template returning entity_id \u2192 brightness, 1-255, for\n            lights that should stay dimly lit when the room is empty,\n            instead of switching off. Its own per-entity values always\n            win over the per-phase settings below - those only fill in\n            entities it doesn't already mention.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, under Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_idle_brightness:\n          name: Morning Idle Brightness (Optional)\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        day_idle_brightness:\n          name: Day Idle Brightness (Optional)\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        evening_idle_brightness:\n          name: Evening Idle Brightness (Optional)\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        night_idle_brightness:\n          name: Night Idle Brightness (Optional)\n          description: >\n            What this phase dims to when the room is empty, instead of\n            switching off, on the same 0-255 scale as the phase\n            brightnesses. 0 means it goes dark, which is the default.\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n    scene_handoff:\n      name: Scene Handoff\n      icon: mdi:palette-swatch\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        scene_template:\n          name: Scene Template (Optional)\n          description: >\n            Template returning a scene entity_id to hand the room over\n            to instead of the adaptive brightness/colour. Takes\n            precedence over the per-phase scenes below whenever it\n            returns one - they're the fallback for phases it doesn't\n            cover.\n            If it reads another entity, add that entity to Additional\n            Triggers, under Triggers, so the room updates as soon as it\n            changes.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: \"\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        morning_scene:\n          name: Morning Scene (Optional)\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        day_scene:\n          name: Day Scene (Optional)\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        evening_scene:\n          name: Evening Scene (Optional)\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n        night_scene:\n          name: Night Scene (Optional)\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    triggers:\n      name: Triggers\n      icon: mdi:lightning-bolt-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        use_area_sensors:\n          name: Sensors From Areas\n          description: >\n            When disabled, occupancy and motion sensors won't be inferred\n            from the areas, floors, devices or labels in Lights & Occupancy.\n            Only explicitly selected sensors will be used.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#triggers).\n          default: true\n          selector:\n            boolean: {}\n        extra_triggers:\n          name: Additional Triggers (Optional)\n          description: >\n            Entities that make the room update as soon as they change, such as\n            an entity Scene Template or Brightness Template depends on. They\n            only adjust lights that are already on, and never switch one on.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#additional-triggers).\n          default: []\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              multiple: true\n    timing:\n      name: Transitions\n      icon: mdi:timer-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        motion_on_transition:\n          name: Motion On Transition\n          description: Transition duration when turning on via motion or a manual run.\n          default: 1\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        motion_off_transition:\n          name: Motion Off Transition\n          description: Transition duration when turning off via motion.\n          default: 15\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        background_transition:\n          name: Background Transition\n          description: Transition duration when the schedule, the scene template, or an Additional Trigger updates - i.e. nothing a person is actively waiting on.\n          default: 5\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n    colour:\n      name: Colour\n      icon: mdi:palette\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        rgb_phases:\n          name: Prefer RGB During\n          description: >\n            Phases to send RGB colour instead of colour temperature, for\n            lights that support it (auto-detected). At the high colour\n            temperatures used during Morning/Day, this can look\n            blue-tinted rather than a clean white, so those phases are\n            off by default - Evening/Night's warmer values don't have\n            that problem.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#colour).\n          default: [Evening, Night]\n          selector:\n            select:\n              options: [Morning, Day, Evening, Night]\n              multiple: true\n\nmode: restart\nmax_exceeded: silent\n\n# Available to triggers and conditions, unlike variables:.\ntrigger_variables:\n  room_target: !input room_target\n  zone: !input zone\n  use_area_sensors: !input use_area_sensors\n\ntrigger:\n  # The schedule's Phase, which fires on a real phase change (and once at\n  # startup), never on an attribute-only update.\n  - id: phase_change\n    trigger: event.received\n    target:\n      device_id: !input schedule\n    options:\n      event_type:\n        - Morning\n        - Day\n        - Evening\n        - Night\n  # The zone's tick, spaced from every other zone's. The curve is flat in\n  # Morning/Night, so phase_change goes quiet there. Also runs self-heal.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: event\n    event_type: flare_tick\n    event_data:\n      device_id: !input zone\n    enabled: \"{{ zone is not none }}\"\n  # Without a zone, the same tick on the minute. Every zone-less room\n  # writes in the same second, which is what zone ticks spread out.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: time_pattern\n    minutes: \"*\"\n    enabled: \"{{ zone is none }}\"\n  - id: extra\n    platform: state\n    entity_id: !input extra_triggers\n  # Occupancy and motion sensors share the ids. Harmless with no sensor of\n  # either kind in the room. With Sensors From Areas off, `condition:` drops\n  # those from sensors not picked by name.\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: occupancy.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: motion.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: occupancy.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: motion.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: recovered\n    platform: template\n    value_template: >\n      {#\n        Runs an ordinary tick as soon as a light becomes reachable, rather\n        than waiting for the next one. \"At least one reachable\", not \"none\n        unavailable\", so a dead entity can't block it; a bulb recovering\n        beside reachable siblings waits for the tick. Can't use `trigger.*`,\n        which isn't in scope here.\n      #}\n      {% set ns = namespace(entities=[], devices=[], areas=[]) %}\n      {% for key in ['entity_id', 'device_id', 'area_id', 'floor_id', 'label_id'] %}\n        {% set v = room_target.get(key, []) %}\n        {% set ids = [v] if v is string else v %}\n        {% if key == 'entity_id' %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'device_id' %}{% set ns.devices = ns.devices + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'area_id' %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'floor_id' %}\n          {% for f in ids %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + floor_areas(f) %}{% endfor %}\n        {% else %}\n          {% for l in ids %}\n            {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + label_entities(l) %}\n            {% set ns.devices = ns.devices + label_devices(l) %}\n            {% set ns.areas = ns.areas + label_areas(l) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n      {% endfor %}\n      {% for d in ns.devices %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + device_entities(d) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% for a in ns.areas %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + area_entities(a) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% set light_entity_ids = ns.entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | unique | list %}\n      {{ light_entity_ids\n         | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n         | list | length > 0 }}\n\nvariables:\n  schedule: !input schedule\n  # The schedule device's one sensor, which carries the curve.\n  adaptive_sensor: >\n    {{ device_entities(schedule) | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.') | first | default(none) }}\n  scene_template: !input scene_template\n  background_transition: !input background_transition\n  motion_on_transition: !input motion_on_transition\n  no_motion_wait: !input no_motion_wait\n  rgb_phases: !input rgb_phases\n  phase: \"{{ states(adaptive_sensor) }}\"\n  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ phase in rgb_phases }}\"\n  script_transition: >\n    {# Slow for background updates; quick for motion or a manual run. #}\n    {% if trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id in ['phase_change', 'tick', 'extra', 'recovered'] %}\n      {{ background_transition }}\n    {% else %}\n      {{ motion_on_transition }}\n    {% endif %}\n  # Nothing triggered this run: \"Run\" was pressed, or automation.trigger\n  # was called. Forces the tick through override protection.\n  manual_run: \"{{ not (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined) }}\"\n  # Entities picked by name in Room Target, as written: the only sensors\n  # that count with Sensors From Areas off.\n  named_entities: >\n    {% set v = room_target.get('entity_id', []) %}\n    {{ [v] if v is string else v }}\n\n# Plain reading of the inputs, so it needs no resolve_target.\ncondition:\n  - alias: \"Not a sensor that Sensors From Areas leaves out\"\n    condition: template\n    value_template: >\n      {{ use_area_sensors or manual_run\n         or trigger.id not in ['motion_on', 'motion_off']\n         or trigger.entity_id in named_entities }}\n\naction:\n  # Room Target as Home Assistant resolves it for an action, which is how a\n  # flare finds its lights too. Everything below works from it, so the\n  # variables that need it are set here rather than before the trigger's\n  # conditions.\n  - alias: \"Find the room's lights and sensors\"\n    action: flare.resolve_target\n    target: !input room_target\n    response_variable: room\n  - alias: \"Work out what the room needs\"\n    variables:\n      room_entities: \"{{ room.entities }}\"\n      # Not a flare's own light, which would pass the room's values on to\n      # every light in it as an override.\n      resolved_entities: >\n        {{ room_entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | list }}\n      # Up here because variables: render top to bottom and the turn-off lists\n      # below need it.\n      template_brightness_levels: !input brightness_template\n      morning_exclude_lights: !input morning_exclude_lights\n      day_exclude_lights: !input day_exclude_lights\n      evening_exclude_lights: !input evening_exclude_lights\n      night_exclude_lights: !input night_exclude_lights\n      phase_exclude_lights: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_exclude_lights, 'Day': day_exclude_lights,\n                    'Evening': evening_exclude_lights, 'Night': night_exclude_lights} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, []) }}\n      # The template wins over the per-phase exclude list. A single number from\n      # the template means every light in the room.\n      template_brightness_map: >\n        {% set t = template_brightness_levels %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0 %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: t | float}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      brightness_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in phase_exclude_lights %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: 0}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_brightness_map) }}\n      # Lights handed off with a null/false level (\"something else owns\n      # this\"), unlike 0 (\"turn off\"). `is sameas false`, since `0 == false`\n      # in Jinja. Excluded from the turn-offs too.\n      hands_off_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for entity_id, level in brightness_levels.items() %}\n          {% if level is none or level is sameas false %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [entity_id] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      brightness: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'brightness') }}\"\n      color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'color_temp') }}\"\n      # None while the sensor is unavailable.\n      rgb_color: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'rgb_color') }}\"\n      # Up here because the turn-off lists below exclude idle lights. Empty\n      # means dark.\n      template_idle_brightness: !input idle_brightness_template\n      morning_idle_brightness: !input morning_idle_brightness\n      day_idle_brightness: !input day_idle_brightness\n      evening_idle_brightness: !input evening_idle_brightness\n      night_idle_brightness: !input night_idle_brightness\n      phase_idle_brightness: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_idle_brightness, 'Day': day_idle_brightness,\n                    'Evening': evening_idle_brightness, 'Night': night_idle_brightness} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, 0) | int }}\n      # Same precedence as brightness_levels.\n      template_idle_map: >\n        {% set t = template_idle_brightness %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0 %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: t | float}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      idle_brightness: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% if phase_idle_brightness %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: phase_idle_brightness}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_idle_map) }}\n      # Lights that stay lit when the room empties. A null level outranks an\n      # idle one.\n      idle_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for e, level in idle_brightness.items() %}\n          {% if level and e in resolved_entities and e not in hands_off_entities %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [e] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      # Minus hands-off lights. Only feeds the motion_off turn-off.\n      reachable_entities: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | list }}\n      turn_off_entities: >\n        {{ reachable_entities | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # Every idle light has a level, so the idle calls need no brightness.\n      idle_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in idle_entities %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: idle_brightness[e]}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.m }}\n      # The room's working occupancy and motion sensors; only those picked by\n      # name with Sensors From Areas off. An unavailable or unknown sensor\n      # isn't one, so a room whose only sensor is dead counts as having none\n      # rather than as empty.\n      room_occupancy_entities: >\n        {% set sensors = (room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'occupancy') | list\n           + room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'motion') | list)\n           | reject('is_state', ['unavailable', 'unknown']) | list %}\n        {{ sensors if use_area_sensors\n           else sensors | select('in', named_entities) | list }}\n      # No occupancy sensor on, or changed, within the Wait time. Hand-written\n      # because occupancy.is_not_detected's `for:` isn't reliable after a\n      # restart. Only `on` counts as occupied, so a sensor left unavailable\n      # can't hold the room on forever. True with no sensors, so callers also\n      # check room_occupancy_entities.\n      occupancy_clear_for_wait: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(all_clear=true) %}\n        {% for e in room_occupancy_entities %}\n          {% if is_state(e, 'on') or\n                (now() - states[e].last_changed).total_seconds() < (no_motion_wait | int) %}\n            {% set ns.all_clear = false %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.all_clear }}\n      # Empty, with lights that stay dimly lit. Suppresses the curve while\n      # idle: an idle light being on makes `occupied`, and so allow_turn_on,\n      # true, which would ramp the nightlight straight back up.\n      room_is_idle: >\n        {{ idle_entities | length > 0\n           and room_occupancy_entities | length > 0\n           and occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\n      occupied: >\n        {# The room is in use if anything is already on. #}\n        {{ resolved_entities | map('states') | select('eq', 'on') | list | count > 0 }}\n      # THE gate for switching a light on: motion, a manual run, or the room\n      # already in use. Only two things may switch a light on:\n      #\n      #   scene.turn_on / flare.apply_lighting - inside default:'s single\n      #     `if allow_turn_on` block.\n      #   flare.apply_lighting for idle brightness - gated on idle_entities and\n      #     occupancy_clear_for_wait instead.\n      #\n      # Anything new that can switch a light on needs one of those gates. The\n      # idle gate must stay narrower than allow_turn_on, and must not be gated\n      # on `occupied`, which an idle light makes true.\n      allow_turn_on: >\n        {{ manual_run\n           or (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id == 'motion_on')\n           or occupied }}\n      # Retried by self-heal. Excludes hands-off and idle lights.\n      entities_still_on: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | select('is_state', 'on')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # The room's entities and every entity on each light's device, for\n      # scene-compatibility checks.\n      scope_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(entities=room_entities) %}\n        {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n          {% set did = device_id(e) %}\n          {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + (device_entities(did) if did else [e]) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.entities | unique | list }}\n      morning_scene: !input morning_scene\n      day_scene: !input day_scene\n      evening_scene: !input evening_scene\n      night_scene: !input night_scene\n      phase_scene: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_scene, 'Day': day_scene, 'Evening': evening_scene, 'Night': night_scene} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase) }}\n      # scene_template wins when it returns a valid scene; a typo or missing\n      # scene counts as nothing. The entity_id shape check has to come first:\n      # states[] raises on a malformed string, aborting the whole run.\n      desired_scene: >\n        {% set candidate = (scene_template | trim) %}\n        {% if candidate and candidate is match('^[a-z0-9_]+\\\\.[a-z0-9_]+$') and states[candidate] is not none %}\n          {{ candidate }}\n        {% elif phase_scene and states[phase_scene] is not none %}\n          {{ phase_scene }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ '' }}\n        {% endif %}\n      # Re-activating a scene every minute would stomp manual changes, so the\n      # tick never does.\n      scene_recheck_due: \"{{ not (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined and trigger.id == 'tick') }}\"\n      # No scene until flare.compute_scene_coverage says otherwise, in default:.\n      scene_coverage: \"{{ {'scene_active': false, 'covered_entities': []} }}\"\n  # Never checks occupancy: an already-on light should follow the curve\n  # regardless. allow_turn_on decides whether lights may come on.\n  #\n  # motion_on stops if there's nothing to do - nothing off and nothing\n  # idle. `idle_entities`, not `room_is_idle`, which is false once motion\n  # starts.\n  - alias: \"Stop a motion_on run with nothing to turn on\"\n    if:\n      - condition: trigger\n        alias: \"Triggered by motion_on\"\n        id: motion_on\n      - condition: template\n        alias: \"Nothing in the room is off, and nothing has an idle level\"\n        value_template: >-\n          {{ resolved_entities | map('states') | select('ne', 'on') | list | count == 0\n             and idle_entities | length == 0 }}\n    then:\n      - stop: \"Nothing to turn on\"\n  - choose:\n      # The cleared triggers' `for:` is per sensor, so they fire once each\n      # sensor's own Wait time is up, even if another saw motion since.\n      - alias: \"Motion timed out and the room is confirmed empty\"\n        conditions:\n          - condition: trigger\n            alias: \"Triggered by motion_off\"\n            id: motion_off\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Every occupancy sensor has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n        sequence:\n          # flare.turn_off records the turn-off as ours, so it isn't read as an\n          # override.\n          - alias: \"Turn off the light(s)\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ turn_off_entities }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n              zone_device_id: !input zone\n          # Idle lights are dimmed instead. Does nothing with no idle brightness.\n          - alias: \"Leave the idle-brightness lights dimly lit\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Room has idle-brightness lights to dim\"\n                value_template: \"{{ idle_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n            then:\n              - action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: !input motion_off_transition\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  zone_device_id: !input zone\n      # Self-heal: on a tick, with the room empty, retry turn-offs that didn't\n      # land. Exclusive of default:, which would work from the same stale list.\n      - alias: \"Self-heal: retry an earlier turn-off that didn't land\"\n        conditions:\n          # phase_change too: moving to a phase with no idle brightness leaves\n          # lights on that no longer read as idle.\n          - condition: trigger\n            alias: \"Triggered by the periodic tick or a phase change\"\n            id:\n              - tick\n              - phase_change\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room has an occupancy sensor to reconcile against\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_occupancy_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n          # Continuously clear for the full Wait time, so a sensor blip can't turn\n          # lights off.\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Occupancy has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Something in the room is still on\"\n            value_template: \"{{ entities_still_on | length > 0 }}\"\n        sequence:\n          - alias: \"Self-heal: retry turning off lights left on with no occupancy\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ entities_still_on }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n              zone_device_id: !input zone\n    default:\n      - alias: \"Work out which lights the scene takes, if there is one\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"A scene is chosen\"\n            value_template: \"{{ desired_scene | length > 0 }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Compute scene coverage (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.compute_scene_coverage\n            data:\n              scene_entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n              scope_entities: \"{{ scope_entities }}\"\n              target_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n            response_variable: scene_coverage\n      # The scene counts only if it exists and everything it covers is in\n      # scope; otherwise FLARE drives every light.\n      - variables:\n          scene_active: \"{{ scene_coverage.scene_active }}\"\n          # Lights handed off this run - to an active scene, or via a\n          # null/false level. They're never written, so their claims are\n          # released instead of going stale into \"overridden\". Lights only: a\n          # scene can set other domains, which hold no claims.\n          handed_off_entities: >\n            {{ ((scene_coverage.covered_entities if scene_active else []) + hands_off_entities)\n               | select('match', 'light[.]') | unique | list }}\n          # No off-light filter: the step using it is already behind\n          # allow_turn_on.\n          target_entities: >\n            {{ scene_coverage.uncovered_entities if scene_active else resolved_entities }}\n      # Everything that can switch a light on is under this gate (see\n      # allow_turn_on). An empty room settles to its idle brightness, outside\n      # the gate. room_occupancy_entities is checked because a room with no\n      # sensors would otherwise always read as empty.\n      - alias: \"Settle an empty room to its idle brightness\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room is idle, and the sensor has a colour target\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_is_idle and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Apply idle brightness (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.apply_lighting\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n              brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n              color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n              rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n              transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n              prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n              zone_device_id: !input zone\n      - alias: \"Only motion, a manual run, or a room already in use may switch a light on\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Allowed to turn on, and not already handled by the idle nightlight\"\n            # Stops the nightlight ramping itself back up (see room_is_idle).\n            value_template: \"{{ allow_turn_on and not room_is_idle }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Activate a scene, if one applies and is due a recheck\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"A scene applies and is due a recheck\"\n                value_template: \"{{ scene_active and scene_recheck_due }}\"\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Activate matching scene\"\n                action: scene.turn_on\n                target:\n                  entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n                data:\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n          # Guarded because the sensor attributes render null when the sensor is\n          # unavailable, and apply_lighting requires both.\n          - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting, unless the sensor has no target to apply\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Sensor has a real brightness and colour target\"\n                value_template: \"{{ brightness is not none and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting (FLARE)\"\n                action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ target_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ brightness_levels }}\"\n                  brightness: \"{{ brightness }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  zone_device_id: !input zone\n                  # A manual run forces the tick through override protection.\n                  force: \"{{ manual_run }}\"\n      # Bookkeeping only, so outside the gate.\n      - alias: \"Release lights handed off to a scene or another owner\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"There are lights to release, in a zone\"\n            value_template: >-\n              {{ zone is not none and handed_off_entities | length > 0 }}\n        then:\n          - action: flare.claims_clear\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ handed_off_entities }}\"\n              zone_device_id: !input zone\n", "tree": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 1, "__end_line__": 836, "value": {"blueprint": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 2, "__end_line__": 312, "value": {"name": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 2, "__end_line__": 2, "value": "FLARE"}, "description": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 3, "__end_line__": 12, "value": "FLARE: phase-based circadian lighting - sets brightness/colour temperature from a FLARE schedule sensor, keeping lights updated as it changes, and turns them off a while after occupancy clears. Full details on every input: [the blueprint reference](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/).\n\nBlueprint version 0.16.0 - the integration raises a repair when a newer one is available.\n"}, "domain": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 13, "__end_line__": 13, "value": "automation"}, "author": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 14, "__end_line__": 14, "value": "Dan Spencer"}, "homeassistant": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 17, "__end_line__": 18, "value": {"min_version": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 17, "__end_line__": 17, "value": "2026.4.0"}}}, "input": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 19, "__end_line__": 312, "value": {"schedule": {"__type__": "map", "__line__": 20, "__end_line__": 30, "value": {"name": {"__type__": "scalar", "__line__": 20, "__end_line__": 20, "value": "Schedule"}, "description": {"